# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   For an app, this should ignore it:
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if one uses a different OS than the other, and lockfile contains
#   hashes that are different for different platforms, then it's recommended to ignore Pipfile.lock.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains platform-specific information and can be excluded or included.
#   If you are building a library, you should probably include it.
#   If you are building an application, you should probably include it.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains platform-specific information and can be excluded or included.
#pdm.lock

# PEP 582; global packages directory, used by pyflow and pdm
__pypackages__/

